tution it could be the catylist to return the country to its republican (no, not the political party!) roots.  &lt;BR/&gt;     The Turkish military has done this service for Turkey numerous times.  When the civilian government gets out of control, allowing terrorism and other self-destructive forces to work, the military takes over the government.  Once the military has the country under control and has restored its governmental foundations, it hands the country back to the civilians.&lt;BR/&gt;   If our military would refuse to go anywhere under any circumstances other than proper constitutional authority, this would go a long way to waking the populace up.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116608000698244692/comments/default/116637393598528697'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/116608000698244692/comments/default/116637393598528697'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/12/hey-take-your-time.html?showComment=1166373900000#c116637393598528697' title=''/><author><name>Neo</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/08839164398247281003</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/12/hey-take-your-time.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-116608000698244692' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/116608000698244692' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1580334153"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="December 17, 2006 at 9:45 AM"/></entry></feed>